-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  agg_call.adam - Aggregates across calls (M3.5i). Win64 passes an
  aggregate of 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes in an integer register, any other size
  as a pointer to a copy the caller makes, and returns one of those sizes
  in rax, any other through a hidden pointer to the caller's slot. Every
  record size 1..17 goes in by value (the callee clobbers its copy: the
  caller's value stays), out as a result, and through (a call's result as
  an argument); five aggregates in one call (the fifth on the stack, each
  from a call's result); a hidden result beside a scalar argument, its
  result assigned back over its own argument; a local's and a module
  variable's initializer from a call; records of int32 fields, static
  arrays and sets in and out; C results through ucrtbase: ldiv (ldiv_t, 8
  bytes, in rax) and lldiv (lldiv_t, 16 bytes, hidden pointer). Values are
  shown through ucrtbase (_i64toa + puts); a bool as 0 / 1.
*******************************************************************************/

